        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Enthalpy change of formation",
            "text": "Standard enthalpy change of formation of a compound is the enthalpy change involved when one mole of the compound is formed from its elements under standard conditions."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "It can be exothermic or endothermic. For instance, ΔH°f for methane is given below."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{C_{(s)} + 2H2_{(g)} -> CH4_{(g)}}\\qquad \\Delta H^\\circ_f = -74.8\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "C(s) + 2H₂(g) → CH₄(g)    ΔH°f = –74.8 kJ mol⁻¹"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
